1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:05,197
This love in my heart,
it will burn on forever.

2
00:00:05,280 --> 00:00:09,037
Granting me courage, I
hope it will never stop.

3
00:00:09,120 --> 00:00:12,177
No matter where you
are, nothing is too far.

4
00:00:12,260 --> 00:00:15,857
With our everlasting bones,
we'll reach it, we are home.

5
00:00:15,940 --> 00:00:22,637
I'm

6
00:00:22,720 --> 00:00:23,917
so truly grateful.

7
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:27,800
I ran into you on that day so long ago.

8
00:00:28,680 --> 00:00:32,397
We laughed every moment
with tears in our eyes.

9
00:00:32,480 --> 00:00:34,860
Till we knew we weren't alone.

10
00:00:36,340 --> 00:00:41,820
The blowing wind came in
and joined us on our way.

11
00:00:43,140 --> 00:00:47,097
And with it I know we'll rise.

12
00:00:47,180 --> 00:00:49,797
We'll be flying up high.

13
00:00:49,880 --> 00:00:52,900
Why, tell me why are you giving up?

14
00:00:53,440 --> 00:00:56,160
Why, tell me why you wanna fight alone?

15
00:00:56,720 --> 00:00:59,620
Hey, what kind of future
do you think you have?

16
00:00:59,880 --> 00:01:03,197
Your dream is already in your hands.

17
00:01:03,280 --> 00:01:06,937
This love in my heart,
it will burn off forever.

18
00:01:07,020 --> 00:01:10,757
Granting me courage, I
hope it will never stop.

19
00:01:10,840 --> 00:01:13,897
I don't matter where you
are, nothing is too far.

20
00:01:13,980 --> 00:01:16,457
With our everlasting
plans, we'll reach it.

21
00:01:16,540 --> 00:01:20,517
We are home from the horizon,
out on the edge of the world.

22
00:01:20,600 --> 00:01:23,497
If there is a place that
I'd want to take you to?

23
00:01:23,580 --> 00:01:24,897
Let's head for it then!

24
00:01:24,980 --> 00:01:28,540
But as for the way we already know.

25
00:01:29,280 --> 00:01:31,620
We promised it long ago.

26
00:01:43,360 --> 00:01:45,317
You scream by your voice.

27
00:01:45,400 --> 00:01:47,237
That can't break through the silence.

28
00:01:47,320 --> 00:01:48,817
Feeling defeated.

29
00:01:48,900 --> 00:01:51,037
It crushes your helpless heart.

30
00:01:51,120 --> 00:01:52,697
I've got your back, I swear.

31
00:01:52,780 --> 00:01:54,177
I'll always be here.

32
00:01:54,260 --> 00:01:57,960
Let's put our fate within
this light under the sun.

33
00:01:58,960 --> 00:02:02,880
Can you close your eyes and
just listen to my voice?

34
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:04,897
Let's find the answer together.

35
00:02:04,980 --> 00:02:07,597
I'm telling you in our path.

36
00:02:07,680 --> 00:02:09,617
I trust that it will lead us.

37
00:02:09,700 --> 00:02:11,517
To another sea untarded.

38
00:02:11,600 --> 00:02:13,417
Cause now we are home.

39
00:02:13,500 --> 00:02:16,147
On the horizon, out on
the edge of the world.

40
00:02:16,720 --> 00:02:19,197
There is a place I want to take you to.

41
00:02:19,280 --> 00:02:20,697
Let's head for it then.

42
00:02:20,780 --> 00:02:24,320
But after the way we already know.

43
00:02:25,240 --> 00:02:27,360
We promised it long ago.

44
00:02:31,920 --> 00:02:33,420
You insolent brat.

45
00:02:34,020 --> 00:02:35,957
Gaze upon my sword with fear!

46
00:02:36,040 --> 00:02:38,100
It's quite splendid, isn't it?

47
00:02:38,280 --> 00:02:42,520
Best remember the name Pretzel You're
seeing a one-of-a-kind masterpiece

48
00:02:43,360 --> 00:02:47,478
It's going to teach you a lesson On
how we run things in the new world

49
00:02:48,080 --> 00:02:48,910
Huh?

50
00:02:49,020 --> 00:02:51,020
How can you call it one of a kind?

51
00:02:51,320 --> 00:02:53,144
Aren't you holding six of them?

52
00:02:55,360 --> 00:02:57,066
Let's get out of here, Luffy.

53
00:02:57,340 --> 00:02:58,400
It's not over.

54
00:02:59,140 --> 00:03:00,100
Let's go!

55
00:03:00,380 --> 00:03:01,260
Third gear!

56
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:04,830
Now!

57
00:03:04,960 --> 00:03:05,860
Gum-Gum!

58
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:09,440
All of them run!

59
00:03:22,320 --> 00:03:25,660
You don't know what you've
gotten into, pathetic.

60
00:03:47,760 --> 00:03:49,560
That's all!

61
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:51,180
No!

62
00:04:27,400 --> 00:04:29,160
That's my brother.

63
00:04:29,720 --> 00:04:30,550
Luffy.

64
00:04:47,940 --> 00:04:51,697
Oh no, don't forget they work for Big Mom.

65
00:04:51,780 --> 00:04:53,897
We really shouldn't take this lightly.

66
00:04:53,980 --> 00:04:58,560
I'm surprised even Luffy's
having a hard time.

67
00:04:59,980 --> 00:05:01,760
Hurry, get up!

68
00:05:05,340 --> 00:05:06,540
What now?

69
00:05:08,860 --> 00:05:11,157
Not so fast, little missy.

70
00:05:11,240 --> 00:05:12,197
I'm still here.

71
00:05:12,280 --> 00:05:14,840
Remember, you can't retreat.

72
00:05:26,640 --> 00:05:27,470
Heat.

73
00:05:36,180 --> 00:05:40,060
Your heart must be pounding in
your throat by now, poor thing.

74
00:05:42,220 --> 00:05:43,840
Worst generation, huh?

75
00:05:44,140 --> 00:05:45,920
I say, whoop-de-doo!

76
00:05:46,280 --> 00:05:50,137
Hope you all had a good time playing
pirates cruising the Grand Line.

77
00:05:50,220 --> 00:05:54,000
I've seen countless faces of
underlings like you come and go,

78
00:05:54,200 --> 00:05:58,697
always spouting the same nonsense that
their captain will be king of the pirates.

79
00:05:58,780 --> 00:06:01,240
You know how that story ends? In despair.

80
00:06:02,040 --> 00:06:05,980
You all wander into Mama's
territory and learn the same lesson.

81
00:06:07,480 --> 00:06:08,980
Captain Kid did.

82
00:06:09,540 --> 00:06:14,940
Also, Roar of the Sea, Apu, Gang
Buggy, and even Mad Monk-Aruge.

83
00:06:15,940 --> 00:06:18,180
Only Buggy recognized the danger.

84
00:06:18,520 --> 00:06:21,640
He had enough wits about
him to join forces with us.

85
00:06:22,060 --> 00:06:25,277
The rest of those pathetic
worst-generation upstarts

86
00:06:25,360 --> 00:06:28,713
were driven away without even
catching a glimpse of Mama.

87
00:06:30,420 --> 00:06:32,660
Well, one of them had some backbone.

88
00:06:33,600 --> 00:06:35,300
That's Mad Monk-Aruge.

89
00:06:36,860 --> 00:06:40,917
The scoundrel was crafty enough to take
down one of our strongest officers.

90
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:45,040
Hard to believe they were the sweet
four generals not so long ago.

91
00:06:47,840 --> 00:06:49,637
That's as far as he made it.

92
00:06:49,720 --> 00:06:53,557
Mama was so furious she sent
brother Cracker to finish the job.

93
00:06:53,640 --> 00:06:56,077
Your friend has nowhere to run.

94
00:06:56,160 --> 00:06:59,880
I imagine he must be taking
his last breath by now?

95
00:07:07,340 --> 00:07:08,440
She's gone.

96
00:07:18,720 --> 00:07:20,160
Listen closely.

97
00:07:20,860 --> 00:07:23,684
You've reached your final
stop in the new world.

98
00:07:30,900 --> 00:07:35,160
You want to fight an
emperor? Really? You fool.

99
00:07:35,300 --> 00:07:37,520
You won't even get close to Mama.

100
00:07:38,880 --> 00:07:42,180
Infiltrating the tea party,
stopping the wedding,

101
00:07:42,760 --> 00:07:46,137
and then walking out of here
alive with your lost Gourmet.

102
00:07:46,220 --> 00:07:48,317
Oh, yeah, like that's
ever going to happen.

103
00:07:48,400 --> 00:07:53,340
This forest will be your final resting
place without ever catching sight of Mama.

104
00:07:57,640 --> 00:07:59,080
No, my climb attacked!

105
00:08:01,740 --> 00:08:03,520
Welcome to Mirror World.

106
00:08:03,760 --> 00:08:05,466
You're going to love it here.

107
00:08:07,520 --> 00:08:09,320
Stop it! Let me go!

108
00:08:11,300 --> 00:08:13,200
Come on. Come on!

109
00:08:13,380 --> 00:08:14,520
Come to old Barrel.

110
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:19,588
I can't wait to carve up that little
face in the comfort of another dimension.

111
00:08:21,060 --> 00:08:22,460
Bound! Help me!

112
00:08:26,260 --> 00:08:27,860
Just give in already.

113
00:08:28,440 --> 00:08:30,480
Let her go, Barrel!

114
00:08:42,820 --> 00:08:44,060
Thanks a bunch.

115
00:08:44,560 --> 00:08:45,800
Are you serious?

116
00:08:46,480 --> 00:08:48,120
Nice going, Pound.

117
00:08:48,340 --> 00:08:50,693
You just committed treason against Mama.

118
00:08:51,060 --> 00:08:52,540
You're dead to us.

119
00:08:52,700 --> 00:08:54,240
And soon, just dead.

120
00:09:05,300 --> 00:09:08,220
Here comes a thunderbolt tempo!

121
00:09:50,080 --> 00:09:53,757
She'll be back as always, huh, well?

122
00:09:53,840 --> 00:09:58,517
You see, her ability lets her appear
pretty much any place that has a mirror.

123
00:09:58,600 --> 00:10:01,797
Sorry, are you in trouble now?

124
00:10:01,880 --> 00:10:04,277
Apparently, I was already in trouble.

125
00:10:04,360 --> 00:10:08,520
Cracker was told to kill me
by none other than Lin-Lin.

126
00:10:09,020 --> 00:10:14,720
Oh, yeah, it just reminded me.

127
00:10:14,980 --> 00:10:17,137
Are you one of Lola's friends, by chance?

128
00:10:17,220 --> 00:10:18,050
Uh-huh.

129
00:10:28,920 --> 00:10:31,700
I would say that officially
settles it, then.

130
00:10:32,420 --> 00:10:34,480
Lola's mother has to be Big Mom.

131
00:10:36,640 --> 00:10:41,405
The fact that the creatures here have such
a reaction to this is proof in itself.

132
00:10:42,540 --> 00:10:45,069
I'll make sure to put
it to good use, Lola.

133
00:11:09,320 --> 00:11:10,220
Oh no!

134
00:11:10,600 --> 00:11:11,835
We're in his pathway!

135
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:26,180
Hey, hold on!

136
00:11:26,400 --> 00:11:29,517
Don't forget we still have a duty
to uphold us the seducing ones!

137
00:11:29,600 --> 00:11:31,860
We can't let anyone escape!

138
00:11:34,680 --> 00:11:35,680
Right!

139
00:11:36,060 --> 00:11:37,220
Plunk is back!

140
00:11:52,800 --> 00:11:54,600
Come on, Kong!

141
00:11:59,600 --> 00:12:01,080
God, my God!

142
00:12:01,460 --> 00:12:02,820
Hard biscuit block!

143
00:12:08,140 --> 00:12:09,500
No good!

144
00:12:09,780 --> 00:12:10,800
Dear guy!

145
00:12:11,320 --> 00:12:13,400
He's using armament Haki!

146
00:12:35,920 --> 00:12:41,220
If you truly care about Vinsmok Sanji as
a friend, surely you should let him go.

147
00:12:41,540 --> 00:12:43,840
He is the prince of a mighty kingdom.

148
00:12:44,340 --> 00:12:47,340
His status far exceeds your own, boy.

149
00:12:49,440 --> 00:12:51,620
By taking a noble wife,

150
00:12:51,880 --> 00:12:56,820
he can enjoy living in luxury
with every desire catered to.

151
00:13:02,700 --> 00:13:05,757
Would you rather selfishly
take your friend back or

152
00:13:05,840 --> 00:13:09,134
allow him to partake in the
happiness he is entitled to?

153
00:13:09,320 --> 00:13:12,700
Compared to his new family,
you're childish and weak.

154
00:13:13,100 --> 00:13:17,335
Can you imagine what a prince would
say looking upon a failure like you?

155
00:13:20,780 --> 00:13:25,000
Get out of my sight, you
wretched low-class pirate!

156
00:13:34,320 --> 00:13:35,150
Karoo!

157
00:13:35,900 --> 00:13:36,880
Karoo!

158
00:13:39,580 --> 00:13:41,300
Karoo! Karoo!

159
00:13:42,340 --> 00:13:44,780
Karoo! Muscle balloon! Let's go!

160
00:13:45,240 --> 00:13:47,120
Ha! Ha!

161
00:14:11,100 --> 00:14:13,280
Fourth gear!

162
00:14:13,940 --> 00:14:15,380
Bounce man!

163
00:14:18,820 --> 00:14:22,644
Muscle Balloon isn't a bad name
coming from a simpleton like you.

164
00:14:24,600 --> 00:14:28,280
But bouncing balls don't exactly
strike fear into my heart.

165
00:14:29,760 --> 00:14:32,120
Let me spell it out one more time.

166
00:14:32,480 --> 00:14:33,640
You're low class.

167
00:14:34,020 --> 00:14:34,961
Go home already!

168
00:14:48,300 --> 00:14:50,817
All right, gum, gum, gum!

169
00:14:50,900 --> 00:14:52,280
Hard biscuit block!

170
00:14:53,040 --> 00:14:54,800
Gah! Gah!

171
00:15:00,260 --> 00:15:01,201
General Cracker!

172
00:15:20,360 --> 00:15:22,680
You don't know Sanji at all!

173
00:15:23,060 --> 00:15:28,500
You insult him, even if he is happy with
his new life and doesn't want to come back!

174
00:15:28,700 --> 00:15:30,800
He'd never talk to us like that!

175
00:15:42,380 --> 00:15:43,680
No, it's not!

176
00:15:43,900 --> 00:15:45,780
Not until I save Sanji!

177
00:15:47,120 --> 00:15:48,800
All right, Kong Kong!

178
00:15:49,540 --> 00:15:51,540
I wouldn't push your luck with me.

179
00:15:53,280 --> 00:15:54,660
Come here!

180
00:15:55,420 --> 00:15:56,500
Kong Kong!

181
00:15:56,600 --> 00:15:57,780
Let's all roll!

182
00:16:04,160 --> 00:16:05,680
General Prattler!

183
00:16:31,640 --> 00:16:33,557
I'll admit that impressed me.

184
00:16:33,640 --> 00:16:35,437
Well done!

185
00:16:35,520 --> 00:16:36,720
Breaking my armor?

186
00:16:42,560 --> 00:16:44,377
And just who are you?

187
00:16:44,460 --> 00:16:46,340
Is that not obvious?

188
00:16:47,600 --> 00:16:52,740
Pretty sure I already introduced myself
as the Sweet Three General Cracker.

189
00:17:01,400 --> 00:17:05,600
That was my favorite armor,
you know. Armor? Liar!

190
00:17:05,700 --> 00:17:07,260
I saw him cough up blood!

191
00:17:07,460 --> 00:17:08,440
That was jam.

192
00:17:09,560 --> 00:17:11,680
I'm a true craftsman at heart.

193
00:17:11,960 --> 00:17:13,800
It even tasted good, too.

194
00:17:16,340 --> 00:17:19,980
After consuming the bis-bis
fruit, I became a biscuit man.

195
00:17:20,400 --> 00:17:24,740
I make infinite amounts of
biscuits and manipulate them.

196
00:17:32,980 --> 00:17:35,200
The possibilities are endless.

197
00:17:36,760 --> 00:17:37,980
Crushed biscuit!

198
00:17:45,560 --> 00:17:48,220
If I can imagine it, I can craft it.

199
00:17:51,080 --> 00:17:53,940
Look familiar, the face
of a hardened warrior.

200
00:17:56,720 --> 00:17:58,779
Much like biscuits through history,

201
00:17:59,020 --> 00:18:02,902
they change shapes based on the
era or the whims of their creator.

202
00:18:04,180 --> 00:18:07,651
Not many people have ever caught
a glimpse of my true self.

203
00:18:09,640 --> 00:18:13,346
Have you seen my wanted poster
that's issued by the government?

204
00:18:14,180 --> 00:18:15,760
That's not my face.

205
00:18:15,980 --> 00:18:17,080
It's my armor.

206
00:18:20,040 --> 00:18:22,480
Frankly, I detest the feeling of pain.

207
00:18:22,820 --> 00:18:24,880
And the same goes for injections.

208
00:18:25,460 --> 00:18:30,500
That's why I surround myself in a suit of
armor and control it to fight in my stead.

209
00:18:30,880 --> 00:18:32,740
It multiplies as I clap.

210
00:18:33,220 --> 00:18:35,691
This is the height of artisanal biscuitry.

211
00:18:36,220 --> 00:18:37,800
A dream come true.

212
00:18:37,980 --> 00:18:40,420
Limitless forces at my disposal!

213
00:18:42,600 --> 00:18:45,977
The one you struggled
so hard to destroy was

214
00:18:46,060 --> 00:18:48,825
but a single biscuit
warrior in a line of many.

215
00:18:48,980 --> 00:18:51,960
I can duplicate them as
many times as I desire.

216
00:18:52,440 --> 00:18:57,200
Now do you understand why you will
never see Vinsmoke Sanji again?

217
00:19:00,280 --> 00:19:01,620
I'll be back.

218
00:19:09,840 --> 00:19:12,680
I'm gonna see Soji! You're wrong!

219
00:19:17,340 --> 00:19:19,820
Truth is, no matter how strong you are,

220
00:19:19,960 --> 00:19:22,557
there are people out
there you can never beat.

221
00:19:22,640 --> 00:19:25,497
Learning to accept that
doesn't mean you've failed.

222
00:19:25,580 --> 00:19:26,520
It's progress.

223
00:19:33,740 --> 00:19:35,360
You still want to fight?

224
00:19:42,000 --> 00:19:43,176
AAAAAAHHHHHHHHHHH!!!

225
00:19:51,540 --> 00:19:53,720
We can't stick around here!

226
00:19:54,180 --> 00:19:57,200
We don't get a chad, noooooooooo!

227
00:20:07,260 --> 00:20:09,200
Hopefully we'll be safe now.

228
00:20:10,200 --> 00:20:12,537
There's really no point
in us sticking around.

229
00:20:12,620 --> 00:20:14,200
Oh, I'm still here.

230
00:20:28,560 --> 00:20:30,080
We can't escape!

231
00:20:32,000 --> 00:20:35,380
You could try it, but
there will be consequences!

232
00:20:40,300 --> 00:20:43,640
I thought I told you all to
help out Luffy with Cracker!

233
00:20:44,200 --> 00:20:47,960
No matter how many of you wither,
it won't bother me one bit!

234
00:20:51,060 --> 00:20:54,340
How could you say something
that awful with a smile?

235
00:20:54,560 --> 00:20:56,537
So you're afraid of General Cracker?

236
00:20:56,620 --> 00:20:58,900
Well, how about Big Mom, then?

237
00:20:59,460 --> 00:21:01,280
Which one is scarier?

238
00:21:01,960 --> 00:21:03,160
You are!

239
00:21:19,300 --> 00:21:20,820
I get it now.

240
00:21:21,260 --> 00:21:23,620
Am I smarter or what? Here, listen.

241
00:21:25,100 --> 00:21:26,997
Listen, I got this all figured out.

242
00:21:27,080 --> 00:21:30,786
From this point on, you can call
me your Big Bro Chopper, okay?

243
00:21:31,900 --> 00:21:33,380
Sure, no problem.

244
00:21:33,900 --> 00:21:34,730
Cool.

245
00:21:34,813 --> 00:21:36,997
Okay, so what's the thing you figured out?

246
00:21:37,080 --> 00:21:39,300
My Cho-Bro, your Cho-Bro.

247
00:21:39,900 --> 00:21:43,900
Yeah, it's short for Big
Bro Chopper. Cho-Bro.

248
00:21:45,300 --> 00:21:47,080
I guess that's okay, too.

249
00:21:48,780 --> 00:21:49,610
Anyway,

250
00:21:49,700 --> 00:21:51,617
it seems like this world
is actually connected

251
00:21:51,700 --> 00:21:54,053
to all the mirrors on Whole Cake Island.

252
00:21:54,480 --> 00:21:56,280
I think you, Tia, are right.

253
00:21:57,180 --> 00:22:01,977
So maybe instead of escaping, we should
use Brule's ability to our advantage.

254
00:22:02,060 --> 00:22:03,680
Sounds good, but how?

255
00:22:04,000 --> 00:22:08,360
Since we can see everything, let's
try to locate Sanji That's brilliant!

256
00:22:08,760 --> 00:22:10,080
Great job, Chobro!

257
00:22:11,800 --> 00:22:16,140
That compliment doesn't make me
happy at all, you little scamp you

258
00:22:27,280 --> 00:22:30,160
Secret song, whirlwind slash.

259
00:22:46,700 --> 00:22:48,400
I'd say that we will.

260
00:22:50,320 --> 00:22:54,037
After their patrol route, the
Biscuit warriors go back to the Shit.

261
00:22:54,120 --> 00:22:55,340
We will strike then.

262
00:23:16,500 --> 00:23:20,920
I'll destroy anything that gets
between me and Sanji, no matter what!

263
00:23:47,920 --> 00:23:50,600
Come on, come, come!

264
00:23:52,480 --> 00:23:54,120
Come on, look out!

265
00:23:54,900 --> 00:23:55,730
Time!

266
00:24:02,580 --> 00:24:03,410
Onward!

267
00:24:08,040 --> 00:24:09,440
Time!

268
00:24:28,660 --> 00:24:29,542
Honey pretzels!

269
00:24:41,260 --> 00:24:42,520
Good morning, Mama!

270
00:24:42,720 --> 00:24:44,637
We have a very busy day ahead of us.

271
00:24:44,720 --> 00:24:45,920
First on the agenda,

272
00:24:46,260 --> 00:24:50,577
the Vinsmoke family will be stopping
by to attend the engagement ceremony.

273
00:24:50,660 --> 00:24:53,307
Do we have an update on
the wedding cake yet?

274
00:24:53,600 --> 00:24:54,840
That comes tomorrow.

275
00:24:57,960 --> 00:25:00,180
An entire night has passed.

276
00:25:00,940 --> 00:25:03,720
How are those irksome little gnats doing?

277
00:25:04,100 --> 00:25:07,280
They have one last chance
to meet with their Gourmet.

278
00:25:07,580 --> 00:25:09,051
Having some doubts, Mama?

279
00:25:09,160 --> 00:25:11,857
You know they don't stand a
chance against General Cracker.

280
00:25:11,940 --> 00:25:16,317
Once Blackleg steps into this
castle, the deed is as good as done.

281
00:25:16,400 --> 00:25:18,677
Their chance of meeting him is zilch.

282
00:25:18,760 --> 00:25:23,397
After all, the tea party and wedding will
both be held within these very walls.

283
00:25:23,480 --> 00:25:26,940
So they're all talk then, like usual.

284
00:25:27,900 --> 00:25:31,640
We're still waiting on a few
Vinsmokes to arrive, right?

285
00:25:31,980 --> 00:25:36,160
Uh, actually, I've received word
that they just landed at the port.

286
00:25:38,540 --> 00:25:40,197
This is good news indeed.

287
00:25:40,280 --> 00:25:43,000
All of my beloved sons are here.

288
00:25:43,720 --> 00:25:47,020
I cannot wait to see
them face off with Sanji.

289
00:26:05,180 --> 00:26:06,500
Welcome back!

290
00:26:31,140 --> 00:26:32,120
Master Nijiji!

291
00:26:32,400 --> 00:26:33,320
Master Nijiji!

292
00:26:33,560 --> 00:26:34,760
It's been a while!

293
00:26:35,160 --> 00:26:38,513
I can't believe they ended
that long war on rock calling!

294
00:26:52,680 --> 00:26:54,798
Why isn't he coming out to greet us?

295
00:26:55,020 --> 00:26:55,940
Where is he?

296
00:26:56,240 --> 00:26:57,380
Knock it off, Niji.
